; One claim-bearing predicate written three ways: the bare scalar the rule
; refuses, the minimal claim which is the whole of the escape hatch, and the
; full claim. The two claims differ only in whether they say how good the
; number is, which is the difference between unrankable and rankable.
(node site:S-101
  (kind Space)
  (type MeetingRoom)
  (geometry area)
  ; Refused. It is one keystroke from correct and reads as a simplification,
  ; which is exactly why it is a load error and not a lint.
  (width 8.5)
  ; The escape hatch: somebody who does not know how good the figure is says
  ; so by leaving the accuracy out, and states the method they do have. It
  ; loads, and it is unrankable.
  (width
    (value 8.4 m)
    (source "Massing study MS-2026-002, sheet 1")
    (method method:estimated)
    (date "2026-01-05"))
  ; The same predicate, measured, with the accuracy written.
  (width
    (value 8.5 m)
    (source "Plan set A-101, sheet 3")
    (method method:scaled-from-plan)
    (accuracy (independent 0.05 m))
    (date "2026-01-09")))
